{
  "title": "Elbow Dislocation - Pediatric",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4013/elbow-dislocation--pediatric",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 16 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Elbow Dislocations in the pediatric population usually occur in older children (10-15 years) and can be associated with elbow fractures such as medial epicondyle fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with plain radiographs of the elbow.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually closed reduction followed by brief immobilization. Open reduction is indicated for dislocations associated with a medial epicondyle fracture with an incarcerated fragment.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**3-6% of all pediatric elbow injuries**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dffemographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**male**:female = 3:1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most common in **10-15 year olds**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "very rare in younger children < 3 years old",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fall onto an **outstretched hand**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**posterior dislocation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "hyperextension, valgus stress, and supination",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**anterior dislocation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "a direct posterior to anterior force on a flexed elbow",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**relatively small coronoid process** in children cannot resist distal and posterior displacement of ulna",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "traumatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**avulsion of the medial epicondyle**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4013/images/fig11.jpg",
                      "caption": "XR-Elbow-AP: shows elbow dislocation with associated avulsion of medial epicondyle"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "medial epicondyle fractures are **the most common associated** fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "incarcerated intra-articular bone fragment may block reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "fractures of proximal radius, olecranon and coronoid process",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "neurovascular injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**brachial artery and median nerve**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "may be stretched over displaced proximal fragment",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**ulnar nerve**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "at risk with associated medial epicondyle avulsions",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "most common neuropraxia",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "congenital",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**dislocation of radial head**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Anatomic classification",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "based on the position of the proximal radio-ulnar joint in relation to the distal humerus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "includes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**posterolateral** (most common)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4013/images/ap_and_lateral_of_elbow_dislocation.jpg",
                      "caption": "X-ray and lateral of a pediatric elbow dislocation with associated medial epicondyle fracture"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "posteromedial",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anterior (rare)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "divergent",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4013/images/divergent_elbow_dislocation.jpg",
                      "caption": "divergent pediatric elbow disloation"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "painful and swollen elbow",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "attempts at motion are painful and restricted",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**elbow held in flexion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "forearm appears to be shortened from the anterior and posterior view",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "distal humerus creates a fullness within the antecubital fossa",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4013/images/clinical_photo_of_elbow_dislocation.jpg",
                      "caption": "posterior elbow dislocation with fullness of the elbow region"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "essential to perform neurovascular examination",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "assess for brachial artery and median/ulnar nerve injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "required views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral radiograph of elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "comparison radiographs of the contralateral elbow may be helpful",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "loss or radiocapitellar and ulnohumeral relationship but maintained radial and ulnar relationship",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "look for fractures of **medial epicondyle,** coronoid, proximal radius",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "\"elbow dislocation\" in very young (<3 years old) most likely represents a distal humerus physeal separation and raises concern for nonaccidental trauma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction, brief immobilization with early range of motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**dislocation that remains stable following reduction**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "indicated in the majority of cases",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "reduction technique (see below)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**should be addressed promptly** as reduction should not be delayed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "brief immobilization",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "immobilization should be minimized to 1- 2 weeks to minimize risk of stiffness",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "early therapy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "encourage early active range of motion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**open dislocation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**incarcerated medial epicondyle** or coronoid process in the joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**failure to obtain or maintain an adequate closed reduction**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "significant joint instability (rare)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Closed reduction technique**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior dislocations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "supine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4013/images/supine_elbow_reduction.jpg",
                      "caption": "clinical photo showing supine elbow reduction"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "closed reduction performed with the elbow flexed in forearm supination using gradual traction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "prone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4013/images/prone_elbow_reduciton.jpg",
                      "caption": "clinical photo of prone elbow reduction"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "forearm hanging from table and anterior directed force on olecranon",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "anterior dislocations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "inline traction to distal forearm with a posteriorly directed force on the forearm and an anteriorly directed force on the distal humerus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "post-reduction films should be reviewed to rule out presence of entrapped bone fragment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4013/images/combo.jpg",
                  "caption": "XR-Elbow-AP and Lateral: demonstrates post-reduction film with incacerated medial epicondyle fracture fragmanet"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "must locate medial epicondyle on post-reduction radiographs to ensure it is not within the joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Open reduction**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "depends on reason for blocked reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**elbow medial approach**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4013/images/8_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": "Incise medial capsule to expose medial epicondyle during medial approach to elbow"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "indicated if medial epicondyle avulsion with incarcerated fragment is blocking reduction",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Stiffness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most commonly **loss of terminal extension**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "due to prolonged immobilization",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Heterotopic ossification**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "vigorous reduction increases risk",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Neurologic injuries**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**usually transient**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**median nerve injury may occur due to nerve entrapment**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**ulnar nerve most commonly affected if associated medial epicondyle fracture occurs**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "V**ascular injury**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "brachial artery may be injured (rare)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Compartment syndrome**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "excessive swelling and immobilization in hyperflexion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Chronic instability (recurrent dislocations)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "associated with coronoid and radial head fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
